{
  "package": "archive/zip",
  "notes": "archive::zip: Go-shaped Reader/ReadCloser/Writer/File/FileHeader with ZIP64 read and write, data descriptors, extended timestamps, preambles, raw copy, registered compressors, UTF-8 flag and CP437 names (non-UTF-8 names decode as CP437 Strings and keep their exact bytes in raw_name/raw_comment; the writer stores those bytes as Go does), and the fs.FS view (Reader implements io::fs::FS); Modified is an instant without Go's zone, CreateHeader copies its header and exposes the updated copy, the DEFLATE compressor streams each member through flate::Writer at level 5 and is byte-identical to Go's, ErrInsecurePath is opt-in (GODEBUG=zipinsecurepath=0 or Reader::with_options); Reader<R> is generic over any ReadAt, including borrows such as &File and &[u8], and Reader::new / with_options return Result<Reader<R>, OpenError<R>> whose InsecurePath variant carries the usable reader (OpenError::into_reader; converting to io::Error drops it)",
